WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:01.471
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.471 --> 00:00:03.210
- [Narrator] These
satellite images show silos

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.050
designed to house

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.500
intercontinental ballistic
missiles or ICBMs,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.900
according to military analysts.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.540
Hundreds have been constructed
in China's desert regions

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.580
in the last couple of years.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.650
The launchpads are one
step in China's growth

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.240
as a Nuclear force,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.360
touted in footage broadcast
by Chinese state media,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.100
and analysts say they're getting closer

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.810
to matching the US' capabilities
across land, sea, and air.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.900
Both countries are unlikely
to deploy nuclear weapons,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.610
but reaching triad capabilities

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.340
enforces China's strength
as a nuclear power.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.350
So we unpack how the US and China's

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.881
current Nuclear arsenals match up.

00:00:39.881 --> 00:00:42.750
(dramatic music)

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.250
Since World War Two, the US

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.050
has been testing nuclear weapons.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.140
This created a decades long lead on China,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.390
but military analysts and US officials

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.030
say China's capabilities
are rapidly growing

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.070
under President Xi Jinping.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.700
China currently has an estimated
inventory of 400 war heads

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.500
but the Pentagon says it's on the path

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.220
to having as many as 1500 by 2035.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.830
Compare that to the US,
which has an operational

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.927
warhead inventory, restricted to 1,550.

00:01:11.927 --> 00:01:13.710
(dramatic music)

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.020
And China's nuclear modernization process

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.350
involves more than increasing
the number of warheads.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.810
The country is also advancing
the types of launchers

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.940
in all three triad areas.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.590
Land-based systems are key

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.350
in that three-pronged nuclear structure.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.380
For China, it's the DF-41, an ICBM

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.830
which defense analysts say could
be deployed in those silos.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.860
The missiles can also be
launched from mobile systems.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.720
And the US military says China

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.350
now has more land-based
launchers than the US.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.010
The DF-41 is likely capable
of carrying three warheads,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.270
defense analysts say,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.540
using what's called a MIRV System.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.822
MIRV enables the weapons

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:55.620
to deliver multiple warheads
for different targets,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.160
dropping them at separate points
along the same trajectory.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.420
And Chinese state officials

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.540
said the missile can
travel up to 9,300 miles,

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.460
making it one of the longest range weapons

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.950
of it's type in Beijing's arsenal.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.010
Compare that with the US
version, the Minuteman Three.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.800
The missile has a range
of over 6,000 miles.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.670
It's also capable of carrying
three warheads using MIRV,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.360
but the US limits it's
systems to only deploy one.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.610
Analysts say that
China's expansion on land

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.650
is partly to do with America's development

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.860
of conventional or non-nuclear weapons.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.230
- The Americans have a military

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.750
that is increasingly emphasizing

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.080
long range conventional precision strike.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.390
- [Narrator] Hans Kristensen
has been studying the status

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:42.750
of US nuclear weapons
since the early 1980s.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.030
- Those types of weapons
that, for many targets,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.590
can hold at risk targets

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.640
that previously needed nuclear
warheads to be held at risk.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.340
And this is in fact a serious
concern for the Chinese

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.810
and one of the reasons, I think,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.120
that they're building
these large silo fields

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.650
deep inside China.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.670
- [Narrator] The Chinese government

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.010
did not respond to a
WSJ request for comment

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.630
on whether the building of the silos

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.240
was tied to American
military advancements.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.620
And a senior Chinese official

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.210
would not confirm the missile silos

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.030
in comments to state TV in 2022.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.500
However, the official did say

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.210
the size of China's nuclear force

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.050
should not be estimated,
based on satellite imagery.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.890
Those silos also reveal a key
issue with land-based systems.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.360
They're visible.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.870
So building nuclear missiles
for submarines, or SSBNs,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.390
is a way to remain incognito.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.180
Defense experts say Beijing's
current underwater fleet

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.490
has some crucial vulnerabilities.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.410
- The Chinese nuclear submarines

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:42.030
are widely believed to be much
noisier than American ones.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.530
- [Narrator] That's Dr. Tong Zhao.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.660
He's been researching
China's nuclear weapons

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.220
for more than 10 years.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.610
- And that would significantly undermine

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.540
the overall survivability
of the Chinese submarines

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.970
and therefore undermine
the overall credibility

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.730
of it's sea-based nuclear deterrence.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.290
- [Narrator] Another
crucial differentiator

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.910
is how far the missiles launched

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.830
from the vessels can travel.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.990
Take China's newest Jin Class submarine

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.350
compared with the latest
US version, the Ohio Class.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.990
This submarine carries
the Trident Two Missile,

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:17.490
which can travel approximately
6,480 nautical miles.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.130
Whereas China's carries JL-2 missiles

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.300
which have a shorter range

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.810
of approximately 3,800 nautical miles.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.720
The JL-2 is sufficient for
China to target Alaska,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.390
Guam and Hawaii from waters near China,

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.220
some military experts say,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.200
but to hit US mainland targets,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.300
Beijing's vessels would
need to be deployed

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.790
farther from China's
coast into the Pacific

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.120
where military experts say
the US has an advantage.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.620
That's because the US has placed

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.930
anti-submarine defenses in the waterway,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.230
limiting China's ability to
travel deep into the waters.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.040
- They can go out and and
take all sorts of positions,

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.080
where are they gonna strike from?

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.320
How close are they gonna
be to the Chinese mainland?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.300
- [Narrator] But China's
ability to strike anywhere

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.950
could come together with the deployment

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.110
of it's new JL-3 system.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.330
The Pentagon says it
has an estimated range

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.120
of over 5,400 nautical miles,

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.350
and would for the first time,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.910
place the west coast of the US

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.000
within incredible striking range of China.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.580
The last piece of a nuclear triad status,

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.410
capabilities in the air.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.060
For China, it may come down to

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.580
the H20 Stealth Strategic Bomber.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.490
It's yet to be unveiled,
but in a 2022 report,

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.960
the pentagons of the aircraft

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.380
would have a range of 6,200 miles.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.450
This could help China to reach previously

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.850
out of range areas of the Western Pacific,

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.190
including this US basin, Guam.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.970
It's unclear when the aircraft
will be ready for deployment.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.850
- Are they already fully
operationally deployed

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:49.850
or are they still going through
testing and readjustments?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.554
We don't know.

00:05:51.554 --> 00:05:52.387
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:05:52.387 --> 00:05:54.150
- [Narrator] In contrast,
the US has already

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.370
released new advancements in the air,

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:00.510
with this B-21 stealth bomber
unveiled in early December.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:02.670
- [Hans] This will be the first
time that the United States

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:06.180
has long range nuclear cruise
missiles on a stealth bomber.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.500
- [Narrator] Military analysts say

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.030
the plane helps to modernize

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.670
the country's large, but aging fleet.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.470
- Even when the Chinese get their

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.170
bomber force up to full snuff,

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.890
it's still not a global strike force

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.390
like the American at all.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.340
- [Narrator] Even with
the US ahead in the air,

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.587
China's growth is likely to continue.

00:06:25.587 --> 00:06:27.720
Experts on world nuclear powers

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.670
say that President Xi Jinping's interest

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.850
in expanding Beijing's
nuclear arsenal has increased

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.978
as China becomes an economic
and political rival to the US.

00:06:36.978 --> 00:06:39.930
- (indistinct) China is able to catch up

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:43.230
with United States in terms of
comprehensive national power.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:48.030
His thinking is the more
desperate the US would become

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:52.230
to contain China, to
make trouble for China.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.030
- [Narrator] While it's extremely unlikely

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.000
either nation will actually
deploy nuclear weapons,

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.970
the Pentagon has said China's
expanding nuclear stockpile

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.210
could negatively impact
global strategic stability.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:06.660
- The prospect of a US
China war over Taiwan

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.723
or another regional flashpoint

00:07:09.723 --> 00:07:13.260
is much realistic than before.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.520
- [Narrator] The Biden administration

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.400
has attempted to reduce the
threat of a nuclear conflict

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.100
by pushing for arms
control talks with China.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.140
But China has rejected those overtures,

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.790
citing it's smaller inventory

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.240
and saying the US should
reduce it's stockpile first.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.610
And military analysts note
that China's expansion

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.770
also comes after decades of criticizing

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:33.720
the United States and Soviet Union

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.240
for possessing nuclear triad status.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.500
- [Dr. Tong Zhao] China sees itself

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.071
as a leading international power

00:07:40.071 --> 00:07:43.950
which deserves to possess
the same capabilities

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.323
as the other nuclear major powers.

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.850
(mellow music)

